// The Appeal, ch12: The Last Move. Wednesday, September 15 to Wednesday, October 27, 2027 (the Wednesday calls from the county jail in Brighton; Federal on Thursday, September 30; Teo's carport that night; the office on Friday, October 1; Consuelo's kitchen on Saturday, October 2; the call on Wednesday, October 6; Federal on Wednesday, October 13; the dismissal on Friday, October 15; the note on Monday, October 18; the last call on Wednesday, October 20; Brighton and the drive home on Friday, October 22; box one on Saturday, October 23; the kitchen on Wednesday, October 27, twenty years to the day).
// Coverage per the bible: scenes LR01x2 LR12 LR04 LR10 LR16 LR14 LR09 RC01 RC04 RC11 RC12; quiz LR01x2 LR12x3 LR04 LR10 LR16 LR14x2 LR09 LR13 RC01 RC08 RC04x2 RC11 RC06.
// Full-length passage (p1): Judge Esquibel's written order of September 30, 2027 (new, fiction), mirroring the 2010 opinion: identification is the order's first subject, and its last paragraph sets the remaining claims aside, vacates the conviction and makes no finding as to who. It carries all six RC quiz items. The order's last paragraph is the scene prop in f12s1.
// Law and practice, story level only. The order applies Ana's ch6 card (NEW. ALL FOUR.), and the ch6 calls make Teo and the boy fail line two because Luis knew (conceded in ch11, recited in the order). The order is dated sixteen days after the hearing, inside the thirty days the ch6 header cites. After the order Luis stays at the county jail in Brighton (ch11). The dismissal is told only as far as the brief allows: Meredith files a one page motion to dismiss on Friday, October 15, says why on the record that afternoon, and the judge signs it the next Thursday; Luis walks out Friday, October 22. No rule numbers. Teo's legal exposure is never stated.
// Weekdays computed 2026-10-17: Wednesday, September 15; Wednesday, September 29; Thursday, September 30; Friday, October 1; Saturday, October 2; Wednesday, October 6; Wednesday, October 13; Friday, October 15; Monday, October 18; Wednesday, October 20; Thursday, October 21; Friday, October 22; Saturday, October 23; Wednesday, October 27, 2027.
// Reveal schedule: the order (f12s1, f12s2), Ana lays it on the 2010 opinion in her drawer (f12s3). Consuelo hears the order read at her table, and her words and Dani's are used right (f12s5, f12s6). Meredith dismisses and never says innocent (f12s9, f12s10). Shannon asks "Then who?" on every path (f12s11). Gene's G.V. note, the book's one "most dangerous sentence," in narration (f12s12). The car, two confessions: Phil's May 2008 offer and the choice between his children, told by Luis first (f12s12), then Dani's doubt (closing). Phil's note read right the next morning (closing prop). Lupe meets her grandfather, the last move, the dishes, the personal statement (closing). The envelope is never crossed out and never shown to Luis. No neck in the car. Luis is never called smaller. The unknown profile stays unnamed.
// Flags set here: none. Read here: usedthesystem (f12s4), wroteshannon (f12s11), calledgenealiar and promisedhim (f12s12), pushedluis, pushedteo and ledconsuelo (closing). The ch2 pick at f2s12 (index 2, "somewhere else at 11:15" under ENOUGH) is read in f12s12, with the same branch ch10 used.
